re memory of the validation/profiling GPUs as remote KV cache storage to eliminate prefix recomputation of speculative generations under limited memory budget. Experiments with two reasoning LLMs on H200 show that SpecGen reduces end-to-end time over three baseline systems, while producing more profiling feedback, increasing resource utilization, and improving kernel speedup under a fixed time and token budget.\nL21: Subjects:  | Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite14†arXiv:2606.17518 [cs.DC]\nL23:    | (or cite15†arXiv:2606.17518v1 [cs.DC] for this version)\nL24:    | cite16†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2606.17518†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Jihu Guo [cite17†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Tue, 16 Jun 2026 04:54:23 UTC (541 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled SpecGen: Accelerating Agentic Kernel Optimization with Speculative Generation, by Jihu Guo and 6 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite12†View PDF L37:   * cite13†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite18†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite19†view license L41: \nL42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.DC\nL45: \nL46: cite20†< prev |   cite21†next > L47: \nL48: cite22†new | cite23†recent | cite24†2026-06 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite25†cs L53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite26†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite27†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite28†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL70: \nL71: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL72: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL75: \nL76: Bibliographic Exp